menu "SpectraLab network manager"

config NET_MGR_NTP_SERVER
    string "NTP server"
    default "pool.ntp.org"
    help
        Fallback time server, used when the DHCP lease does not advertise one.

        The board has no RTC, so without a time source every file it writes
        carries the 1980 FAT epoch instead of a real date. A server advertised
        by DHCP is always preferred, which is what makes this work on a LAN
        with no route to the public internet.

endmenu
